# Worker: Local DevEx & Launch

## Goal (Master-aligned)

Keep the dual-process local stack healthy so investigators can run **Intake → Compare → Report**: UI `http://localhost:5173`, API `http://127.0.0.1:8000`. Prefer `Launch.bat` or **WACMAKR: Full stack** (Node-spawned API; no debugpy).

## Role boundary

**Own:** `Launch.bat`, `setup-local.bat`, `start-*.bat` / `start-local.bat`, `.vscode/launch.json`, `.vscode/tasks.json` — ports, process spawn, health verify paths.

**Do not own:** OAuth/auth logic, LLM provider config, IR/corpus/eval code, product UI beyond “app loads / login reachable.”

## Invariants

- Dual process: Vite UI `:5173` + FastAPI/uvicorn `:8000`
- Prefer Node-spawned uvicorn over `debugpy` (Cursor may lack Python debug extension)
- Never embed real API keys, tokens, or `backend/.env` contents in bat/launch/tasks
- Port cleanup on 8000/5173 is intentional but disruptive — document clearly
- Setup scripts must leave IR path runnable without inventing secrets

## Anti-goals

- debugpy-first or Python-extension-required default launch
- Single-process “API serves UI” as the primary local path
- Hardcoding credentials, SMTP, or Groq/Gemini keys into launch files
- Optimizing for legacy analyzer dashboards over IR workflow startup

## Success criteria

- Full stack starts without unsupported debug types
- Verify: UI login page + `GET http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/health`
- Investigators can reach Intake → Compare → Report after launch

## Escalation map

| Symptom | Escalate to |
|---------|-------------|
| Login / OAuth / redirect / roles | Identity Admin |
| `.env` shape, Groq/Ollama 403/404 | Investigator LLM |
| App loads but stepper/WAC UI broken | Intake UX |
| Cases/export after login | Case Review |
| Accuracy scripts / pytest runners only | Accuracy & Eval |

